# The packaged desktop app (`vite build --mode desktop`, run by `tauri build`).
# Its window is served from http://localhost:31440 by the app itself
# (tauri-plugin-localhost). The server below is the default; a person can
# point the app at another from the sign-in page (its Server line), which is
# kept on the device.
#
# The page and the server are different origins either way, so the app uses
# the bearer transport (apps/client/src/lib/api.ts): sign-in returns a session
# it sends as an Authorization header, and each socket opens with a one-time
# ticket. That works for a server on this computer and for a hosted one; the
# server's CORS admits http://localhost:<port> already.
VITE_FOUNDATION_SERVER=http://localhost:4410
